{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## PLAN REVIEW PASSED (0 blocking, 1 advisory) — attestation certified. **CLAIMABLE NOW.**\n\nThis is the **only story in epic e369 that can be worked in parallel right now.** Every other child fast-fails `review-plan` as `INDETERMINATE` until its prerequisites close; J5 has no unclosed prerequisite.\n\nIts earlier `stale-code` drift (a `Makefile` dependency change) was cleared by the fresh review.\n\nTo pick it up: `rebar claim c97f-90ae-4976-47c7 --assignee <you>` — note the **parent-first cascade** is already satisfied, since epic `e369` is claimed and `in_progress`.\n\nSuggested worktree: reuse `/Users/joeoakhart/rebar-jira-family` (branch `jira-family-seam`, own `.venv` with an editable rebar-HEAD install) **or** cut a fresh one from `origin/main`. Either way prefix commands with `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\"` so the pre-commit hook finds ruff/mypy.\n\nOne consistency note from the epic's plan review: the epic body now names this story's exact image and rationale — `pycontribs/jira-test-image:8.17.1` at `http://localhost:2990/jira`, chosen because 8.17.1 is >= 8.14 (the release that introduced PATs), with the version-drift limitation tracked at `9895-ac7d-4276-4f08`. That matches this story; no change needed here.\n\nAlso relevant to your implementation: the epic now **requires `https` for the DC `base_url` unless `allow_insecure = true`**. Because this harness serves plain HTTP on loopback, the live tests that consume it (J6/J7) must set `allow_insecure = true` explicitly and assert the warning fires — the harness is the *intended* override case, not a bypass."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785338296107580001,"uuid":"c61382c3-10c5-4de0-90b3-dd5dc99a5ffe"}